    "id": "chunk-kb-adr-rel-03",
    "content": "ARCHITECTURAL DECISION RECORD // ADR-REL-03: Mandatory Human Governance Authorization Design\nCase Study: CS-04 (AI Application Reliability: Fisher Information Covariance-Based Abstention & Cryptographic Human Authorization)\nProject ID: proj-ai-reliability (Slug: ai-reliability)\nStatus: ACCEPTED\nAnchor: #adr-rel-03\nPublication Eligibility: PUBLIC_OPEN_SOURCE\n\nDecision & Technical Details:\nIn the documented architecture, agents possess authority to diagnose and recommend, but the application authorization design requires role-based human approval tokens for consequential code-modification or pull-request actions. Consequential patch-writing tools are designed to reject execution without valid human approval tokens.\n",
