    "id": "chunk-kb-adr-solace-01",
    "content": "ARCHITECTURAL DECISION RECORD // ADR-SOLACE-01: Application-Level Ephemeral Buffering Design\nCase Study: CS-05 (Solace AI: Cross-Platform Real-Time Voice Streaming & Application-Level Audio Buffer Handling)\nProject ID: proj-solace-ai (Slug: solace-ai)\nStatus: ACCEPTED\nAnchor: #adr-solace-01\nPublication Eligibility: PUBLIC_OPEN_SOURCE\n\nDecision & Technical Details:\nThe documented implementation design specifies that raw microphone audio is processed as streaming PCM frames in application-managed memory and that buffers are cleared or released through application-level hooks upon completed playback turns. The actual implementation and cleanup behavior across all execution paths were not independently inspected during this Portfolio pass. Termination edge cases (such as mid-stream network dropouts, unhandled exceptions, interrupted playback, or abrupt WebSocket disconnects) have not been independently verified for residual buffer cleanup, and teardown paths across every execution flow have not been independently inspected.\n\nMANDATORY GOVERNANCE CAVEATS:\n• Recorded in React Native Jest test runners in external repository (aadil-lang/solace-ai). Unexecuted in this local repository. Does NOT represent physical Android mobile device hardware or emulator execution.",
