    "id": "chunk-kb-pattern-01",
    "content": "CROSS-PROJECT ENGINEERING PATTERN 01 // Deterministic Non-LLM Processing and Validation\nPattern ID: PATTERN-01\nCategory: Recurring Architectural Principle\nSource: research/engineering/ENGINEERING_EXPERIENCE_KNOWLEDGE_BASE_DRAFT.md#cross-project-patterns\n\nDescription & Engineering Implementations:\nMoving explicitly specified checks and deterministic operations outside probabilistic model generation. Its latency, coverage, and cost depend on the particular implementation and execution environment. For example, VM Copy's Tier-1 in-memory regex and AST evaluator (`lib/eval-layer.ts`) was reported to execute in $<1\\text{ms}$ in-memory at $\\$0$ marginal API spend for the Tier-1 deterministic evaluation gate while upstream LLM generation takes 4–8 seconds (historical observation); other systems (such as EDA CAD closed-form mechanics or Ask Aadil deterministic transcript assembly) have their own distinct execution characteristics and environments. Deterministic operations enforce explicitly codified invariants, but do not eliminate all operational or domain errors.\n\nMANDATORY GOVERNANCE CAVEATS:\n• Applies strictly to Tier-1 in-memory regex and AST deterministic evaluation gate (lib/eval-layer.ts). Upstream generative LLM inference takes ~4–8 seconds (historical observation) and incurs standard provider API costs. Does NOT describe end-to-end generation latency or imply the entire workflow is free.",
