    "id": "chunk-kb-pattern-03",
    "content": "CROSS-PROJECT ENGINEERING PATTERN 03 // Safe Abstention on Ambiguity\nPattern ID: PATTERN-03\nCategory: Recurring Architectural Principle\nSource: research/engineering/ENGINEERING_EXPERIENCE_KNOWLEDGE_BASE_DRAFT.md#cross-project-patterns\n\nDescription & Engineering Implementations:\nEmbodying the principle that \"abstaining from action is superior to executing an incorrect action\" (e.g. `MaterialKnowledgeBase` blocking execution on generic alloy terms; the documented Fisher covariance parameter-uncertainty abstention design in AI Reliability). Safe abstention provides an explicit boundary for uncertain conditions, but the Fisher covariance method represents a documented parameter-uncertainty-based abstention design rather than an independently reproduced execution result or calibrated measure of general LLM confidence in this Portfolio workspace.\n\nMANDATORY GOVERNANCE CAVEATS:\n• Safe abstention parameter bounds (e.g. Fisher covariance in AI Reliability) represent a documented mathematical design, not a locally verified runtime execution in this workspace.",
