    "id": "chunk-kb-pattern-05",
    "content": "CROSS-PROJECT ENGINEERING PATTERN 05 // Failure Isolation via Explicit Boundaries\nPattern ID: PATTERN-05\nCategory: Recurring Architectural Principle\nSource: research/engineering/ENGINEERING_EXPERIENCE_KNOWLEDGE_BASE_DRAFT.md#cross-project-patterns\n\nDescription & Engineering Implementations:\nEmploying distinct failure-isolation mechanisms suited to different domains: asynchronous data quarantine queues (`manual_review.json` dead-letter workflow in ETL) can help isolate non-conforming records from relational stores, whereas client-side state latches (`hasSubmittedRef` in Ask Aadil) isolate speech events to prevent duplicate turn dispatches under tested conditions.\n",
